FILES
       /usr/lib/libc.a     the library
       /usr/lib/crt0.o     the start-up code
       /usr/include        the headers

SEE ALSO
       cc(1), ld(1), ar(1), intro(2)

BUGS
       The library is small. Missing, among much else: getopt, wide
       characters, termios, floating-point exception flags. There
       is one locale, "C" (setlocale(3)).

       A few functions are in libc.a without a declaration in the
       installed headers, so a program must declare them itself:
       rename(const char *, const char *), uname(char *), and,
       because sys/mount.h, sys/ptrace.h and sys/sysinfo.h are not
       installed in /usr/include, mount, umount, ptrace and sysinfo.
       gtty and stty (sgtty.h) are ioctl(2) with TIOCGETP and
       TIOCSETP.
